cff-version: 1.2.0
title: 'CCA: Convergent Context Architecture'
message: 'If you use CCA, please cite it using the metadata below.'
type: software
version: '1.4.0'
date-released: '2026-11-06'
authors:
  - given-names: Jonathan
    family-names: Di Rico
repository-code: 'https://github.com/yonasuriv/CCA'
url: 'https://github.com/yonasuriv/CCA'
abstract: >-
  CCA is an agent-agnostic interoperability architecture for
  filesystem-native AI context, designed to make ICM workspaces,
  LLM Wikis, AGENTS.md, Agent Skills, existing projects, and human
  knowledge-work systems interoperable without forcing a new competing
  convention. It defines stable semantic roles, scoped boundaries,
  configurable bindings, routing, and compatibility rules so durable
  context remains portable across agents, tools, and runtimes.
